Gate nitroo's CUDA build steps on the prover feature.

Part of the verifier-only build of SASH eb95bfa that the SP1 segment guest runs
(verifiable-inference-ethereum SPEC.md §1.1). Upstream source is Apache-2.0;
this patch modifies it (Apache-2.0 §4(b)).

- nitroo/crates/stwo/build.rs ran CUDA cmake on every non-macOS host, whatever
  the features, and its macOS `exit(0)` left unreachable code that nitroo's
  -Dwarnings rejects. It now returns before cmake on macOS and whenever the
  `prover` feature is off (CARGO_FEATURE_PROVER unset).
- nitroo/crates/constraint-framework/src/lib.rs declared `mod cuda_domain` and
  re-exported `CudaDomainEvaluator` unconditionally, and cuda_domain.rs imports
  stwo::prover. Both are now gated on `prover`.

--- a/nitroo/crates/constraint-framework/src/lib.rs
+++ b/nitroo/crates/constraint-framework/src/lib.rs
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 /// ! This module contains helpers to express and use constraints for components.
 mod component;
+#[cfg(feature = "prover")]
 mod cuda_domain;
 
 #[cfg(feature = "prover")]
@@ -19,6 +20,7 @@
 use core::ops::{Add, AddAssign, Mul, Neg, Sub};
 
 pub use component::{FrameworkComponent, FrameworkEval, TraceLocationAllocator};
+#[cfg(feature = "prover")]
 pub use cuda_domain::CudaDomainEvaluator;
 pub use info::InfoEvaluator;
 use num_traits::{One, Zero};
--- a/nitroo/crates/stwo/build.rs
+++ b/nitroo/crates/stwo/build.rs
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 use std::path::PathBuf;
 fn main() {
-    #[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
-    std::process::exit(0);
+    if cfg!(target_os = "macos") || std::env::var_os("CARGO_FEATURE_PROVER").is_none() {
+        return;
+    }
     let dst = cmake::Config::new("src/stwo_cuda/cuda")
         .profile("Release")
         .build_arg("--jobs=16")
